<title>UK: Argentina sets 600 billion lire 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Argentina sets 600 billion lire 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Chase and Banca Commerciale Italiana.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ARGENTINA</p>
<p> AMT    600 BLN LIRE  COUPON     10.0	MATURITY    03.JAN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.75    PAY DATE    03.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.45     SPREAD	+276 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB-	 DENOMS (M) FIVE	SALE LIMS US/UK/IT/AR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  ARGENTIN  TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.75 PCT NOVEMBER 2006 BTP</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
